# danielpauls — Daniel Pauls' entire conversation, every quest he appears in.
#
# A quests/dialogue/ file: DIALOGUE blocks and NO QUEST block. The importer and
# Tools -> Content -> Validate Quests both refuse either mistake. See
# docs/reference/QUEST_TEXT_FORMAT.md.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS DANIEL PAULS' CONVERSATION. One DIALOGUE block per npcId across the whole
# quests/ tree: each import regenerates Dialogue_danielpauls.asset wholesale, so a second file
# declaring DIALOGUE danielpauls would clobber this one. Every future Daniel Pauls quest adds its
# nodes HERE, gated on its own quest id.
#
# The quests whose beats live in this file:
#   spark_of_talent        - quests/spark_of_talent.quest        (granted and completed here)
#   daniel_pauls_quest_one - quests/daniel_pauls_quest_one.quest (completed here; granted by
#                            Councillor Mosley, quests/dialogue/councillormosley.quest)
#   check_out_the_church   - quests/check_out_the_church.quest   (granted here at dpq1_speed;
#                            completed here at cotc_scrapman)
#
# The "done" node is the post-quest state and is expected to grow: as Daniel gains more quests,
# add a new gated choice on NODE start rather than rewriting his farewell.
#
# ⚠ TWO PLAYER LINES ARE THE OWNER'S TO WRITE, both marked  [TODO: ]  :
#   NODE start     - the choice that opens the check_out_the_church branch
#   NODE cotc_show - the click that advances after "What is this contraption?" (script: says nothing)
# The script gives Daniel's lines for this beat but not the player's clicks. Nothing here invents them.
#
# Requires the ActiveAtStage gate and the TEACHSPARK directive — see
# docs/reference/QUEST_TEXT_FORMAT.md.

DIALOGUE danielpauls

# Daniel opens with the same line at every beat; which branch is offered depends on quest state.
# The four spark_of_talent gates are mutually exclusive, so exactly one of THEM can ever be
# visible at once. The daniel_pauls_quest_one gate is not exclusive with them: that quest is only
# granted once spark_of_talent is complete, so while it is active the player sees its branch and
# the post-spark farewell together.
NODE start
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: David Blaine was my 3rd ever student. Second was a fella named Jesus. Now he didn't learn too much, I didn't know spanish and he wasn't great with English but he was a good trier.
CHOICE Uh what? -> offer_open
GATE: not-started spark_of_talent
CHOICE Okay okay! -> nudge
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 0
CHOICE Cheers I guess. -> reward
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 1
CHOICE Fine. -> done
GATE: complete spark_of_talent
CHOICE Hey up. -> dpq1_open
GATE: active daniel_pauls_quest_one
# check_out_the_church branch. Requires the makeshift vape (greys until carried), so it only opens
# once the player is back from the church with it. [TODO: ] is the owner's - Daniel speaks first
# ("What is this contraption?"), so the script never wrote the player's opening click.
CHOICE [TODO: ] -> cotc_show
GATE: active check_out_the_church
ITEM: makeshift_vape x1
CHOICE End Conversation.

NODE offer_open
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: HEY YOU! I can sense it, you've got it. Do me a favour and I'll change your life!
CHOICE What you on about? What you up to? -> research
CHOICE Not now, weirdo.

NODE research
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: There's been a few suspect events. Sparks and bangs, strange folk acting aloof.
CHOICE Actually — saw a bloke get zapped by some smackhead by the Jones' last week. Thought I'd had some dodgy bud. -> sendoff
GRANT: spark_of_talent
CHOICE Right. I'll leave you to it.

NODE sendoff
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Haha! That wasn't the bud, son. That was magic. Please, do me a kindness. Find the oddball and have a word for me.

NODE nudge
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Come on! Get after him!

NODE reward
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Let's have it! I knew you had it in you, you've got the gift!
CHOICE So... what happens now? -> teach
# Gated to stage 1 so it cannot be re-picked once the quest completes (which would reopen the
# naming popup). The reward node is only reachable at stage 1 anyway; this makes the rule the
# validator checks explicit rather than relying on the entry gate.
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 1
TEACHSPARK
COMPLETE: spark_of_talent

NODE teach
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Right, now I invoke the 7 secret corners of the magic circle....... GUH........ feel that? Give it a name if you want, then shout it out and try it!

NODE done
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Careful where you sling spells lad. Johnny Law comes a knocking if you're to liberal with the lightening.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# daniel_pauls_quest_one - "Find the Magic Man".
#
# Reached from NODE start's  GATE: active daniel_pauls_quest_one  choice. The quest itself is
# granted by Councillor Mosley at his hand-in (quests/dialogue/councillormosley.quest, node
# nag_two), never here, and its definition is quests/daniel_pauls_quest_one.quest - one MANUAL
# stage, which nothing watches, so the COMPLETE: below is the only thing that can end it.
#
# One straight run of single-choice nodes: Daniel talks, the player prompts him on.

NODE dpq1_open
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Just the man. Right, well... I know you feel like you're only one now.
CHOICE Do I? -> dpq1_help

NODE dpq1_help
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Well, there's a way you can help me out.
CHOICE Go on. -> dpq1_church

NODE dpq1_church
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: The abandoned church next to the castle has had its copper stripped from the roof.
CHOICE And that's out of the ordinary? -> dpq1_speed

NODE dpq1_speed
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: No. Well, yes. But... it's the speed. I was there just the day before. Then by the morning, poof.
# This one choice both completes "Find the Magic Man" and grants Quest 3, "Check Out the Church" -
# the same shape as councillormosley.quest's nag_two, which completes one quest and grants the next
# from a single choice. By the time Daniel says his closing line, the journal has swapped one quest
# for the next, so it clears as he briefs you rather than a beat later.
CHOICE Maybe it was a gang? -> dpq1_close
COMPLETE: daniel_pauls_quest_one
GRANT: check_out_the_church

NODE dpq1_close
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: It's too big a church... something ain't right. Check it out for me, please. Few quid in it for you too.
# This choice must have no  ->  : that is what ends a conversation. Without one this node has no
# exit, and DialogueManager would append its own - an ending nobody wrote, mid-conversation.
CHOICE Ugh fine.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# check_out_the_church - "Check Out the Church" (Quest 3).
#
# Reached from NODE start's  GATE: active check_out_the_church  choice (which also requires the
# makeshift vape). The player has fought through the church and is showing Daniel what a Neek was
# carrying. The vape is NOT consumed - it travels on to Scrap Man in the Quest 4 arc.

NODE cotc_show
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: What is this contraption?
# [TODO: ] is the owner's. The script has the player say nothing here - just a click onward - but
# the button still needs text. Do not invent it.
CHOICE [TODO: ] -> cotc_scrapman

NODE cotc_scrapman
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Give Scrap Man a shout for me. He might know about this.
# QUEST 4 GOES HERE. This choice completes Quest 3. Once the Quest 4 arc is authored, its first
# quest is granted from this same choice - add  GRANT: investigate_weird_vape  on the line below the
# COMPLETE:, the same shape as dpq1_speed above. Left off for now so no GRANT points at a quest file
# that does not exist yet.
CHOICE Alright.
COMPLETE: check_out_the_church
